  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through next Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe afternoon, a cold front is moving through from north to\nsouth, but bringing no precipitation and just some clouds. \nMeanwhile, a strong Noreaster is passing south/southeast of our \narea and helping to bring some increased winds and seas, but no \nprecipitation. \n\nBreezy and chilly conditions tonight into Friday, and then high\npressure builds in Friday night allowing for lighter winds, with\ncool nights but comfortable days over the weekend.\n\nThe next cold front comes Monday, but like the cold front today,\nit very likely will contain little if any precipitation. Look \nfor chilly temperatures behind the front Tuesday/Wednesday with \nhigh pressure settling in. The prolonged dry spell is very \nlikely to persist into Thursday of next week.",
